QuestGuidance.Register("es",234,{
[7457]="70048C9C\n1\tDefeat the Kala-gijak messenger\tThe Kala-gijak messenger can be found travelling on the path east of Kala-gijak. You should defeat him and intercept any orders he carries.\n2\tCollect orders from Seregost\tThe Kala-gijak messenger can be found travelling on the path east of Kala-gijak. You should defeat him and intercept any orders he carries.\n3\tHabla con Faeron\tFaeron can be found outside the mountain pass in Agarnaith. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[7458]="700529E6\n1\tDefeat frost-bound hobgoblins (total: 5)\tFrost-bound hobgoblins have taken up residence inside Goblin-town, and now they claim to lead the goblins there. You should defeat any frost-bound hobgoblins you find.\n2\tCompletado\tYou defeated a number of frost-bound hobgoblins.\n",
[7459]="70045E55\n1\tTalk to Pippin among the barrows\tIs that Pippin? What is he doing in the Barrow-downs?\n2\tLook for Pippin to the south-east, among the barrows\tPippin was here, but now he is gone. Look for him to the south-east, somewhere among the barrows.\n3\tTalk to Sam among the barrows\tWhat is Sam Gamgee doing here in among the barrows? Where is Frodo?\n4\tFind your friend to the north, among the barrows\tIs that Pippin? You see someone back to the west, among the barrows!\n5\tLoneliness grips your heart\tYour friends have all gone.\n6\tTalk to Uglúk\tYou remember these Orcs... but where is Pippin?\n7\tRun with the Orcs\tYour friends have all gone.\n8\tFind Pippin\tYour friends have all gone.\n9\tDo any of the Rohirrim still live?\t\n10\tHabla con Éowyn\030Talk to Dernhelm\tWho has come to this camp among all the dead?\n11\tDeath hangs above all\tDeath hangs above all.\n12\tSave Éowyn\tDeath hangs above all.\n",
[7460]="70045E5F\n1\tTalk to Pippin in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing\tPippin is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n2\tExamine Merry and complete 'Interlude: A Dream of Cold and Silence'\tMerry suffers from a malady the Gondorians call the Black Shadow. He is on a bed in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, still caught in the throes of a terrible dream from which he cannot wake.\n3\tTalk to Pippin in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing\tPippin is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n",
[7461]="70045E56\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the city\tMithrandir has come down out of the city to speak with you.\n2\tSneak through the city to the Houses of Healing\tPass through the gates and make your way up through Minas Tirith to the Houses of Healing without being seen by Knowing Scholars who might see through your disguise. Esta etapa incluye condiciones de fallo; revisa el diario antes de elegir objetos o acciones.\n3\tTalk to Imrahil outside the Houses of Healing\tPrince Imrahil of Dol Amroth is outside the Houses of Healing.\n4\tEnter the Houses of Healing with Imrahil and Mithrandir\tYou have entered the Houses of Healing at the behest of Mithrandir.\n5\tExamine Faramir in the Houses of Healing\tFaramir is in the south-eastern sick-room of the Houses of Healing.\n6\tExamine Éowyn in the Houses of Healing\tÉowyn is lying in a bed two rooms to the north of Faramir's room in the Houses of Healing.\n7\tExamine Merry in the Houses of Healing\tMerry is in the north-western room of the Houses of Healing.\n8\tAsk Ioreth for athelas\tIoreth might know where you can find some athelas.\n9\tAsk Ioreth for kingsfoil\tIoreth has never heard of athelas. Could it be she would know it by another name?\n10\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Houses of Healing\tMithrandir is in the Houses of Healing.\n",
[7462]="70045E60\n1\tTalk to Ioreth in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing\tIoreth is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing\tGandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf and complete 'Interlude: A Secret Return'\tGandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing\tGandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n",
[7463]="70059DF9\n1\tAyuda a Glóin con 'Sangre de Azog: Una lección aprendida a la fuerza'\tGlóin se encuentra en la sala de guerra de Annâk-khurfu, en Valle Ancestral.\n2\tAyuda al príncipe Durin con 'Sangre de Azog: Padres e hijos'\tEl príncipe Durin se encuentra en la sala de guerra de Annâk-khurfu, en Valle Ancestral.\n3\tAyuda al rey Thorin con 'Sangre de Azog: Hermanos de ayer y de hoy'\tEl rey Thorin se encuentra en el Salón Bajo la Montaña en Erebor.\n4\tAyuda a Hersegg con 'Sangre de Azog: La sexta guerra'\tHersegg se encuentra en Akrâz-zahar, en Erebor.\n5\tAyuda al rey Thorin con 'Sangre de Azog: Reunión en el Hogar de la Montaña'\tEl rey Thorin se encuentra en el Salón Bajo la Montaña en Erebor.\n6\tAyuda al rey Thorin con 'Sangre de Azog: La voluntad de Martillotormenta'\tEl rey Thorin se encuentra en el Salón Bajo la Montaña en Erebor.\n7\tAyuda a Hermáth Martillotormenta con 'Sangre de Azog: La séptima luz'\tHermáth Martillotormenta se encuentra en Vosh Torú, en las salas de residencia de Erebor.\n8\tHabla con Durin en Annâk-khurfu\tDurin se encuentra en la sala de guerra de Annâk-khurfu. Después de hablar con Hermáth Martillotormenta, Durin ha decidido que los Gabil'akkâ marcharán sobre el monte Gundabad en siete días. Debes hablar con Durin.\n",
[7464]="700339A3\n1\tTalk to Helchon\tYou and Helchon have come to the Mournshaws in search of answers, but the journey is wearing on the young Ranger.\n2\tTalk to Helchon\tHelchon is exhausted. The frequent attacks by corrupted creatures have drained his desire to proceed.\n3\tSlowly approach the majestic stag\tA majestic stag has appeared in the forest of the Mournshaws.\n4\tFollow the stag deeper into the forest\tThe majestic stag is leading you deeper into the forest.\n5\tTalk to the mighty figure of the Huntsman\tThe Huntsman awaits your request, Calenglad.\n6\tTalk to Helchon in the Hall of the Huntsman\tHelchon is somewhere in the Hall of the Huntsman.\n",
[7465]="700339A6\n1\tHabla con Prestadír\tPrestadír has woken you for your turn at watch.\n2\tStand watch until dawn\tIt is now your turn to keep watch while the rest of the Grey Company sleeps. You will waken Halbarad at the dawn.\n3\tInvestigate your uneasy feeling\tDid you see something move in the darkness?\n4\tYou need to wake up your comrades before the attack!\t\n5\tTalk to Halbarad and prepare for the Falcon Clan attack\tHalbarad has instructions for you, and you should receive them quickly! The Falcon Clan attack is imminent!\n6\tHabla con Halbarad\tHalbarad is waiting to speak with you following the attack by the Falcon Clan.\n",
[7466]="700339A7\n1\tTalk to Bounder Primstone in the Greenfields\tBounder Primstone is in the Greenfields, waiting for you to walk with him to Oatbarton.\n2\tHabla con el Frontero Primstone\tIt is getting late, and you are not yet at Oatbarton. Bounder Primstone wants to take a short rest.\n3\tHabla con el Frontero Primstone\tYou have walked with Bounder Primstone about halfway to Oatbarton, but you have heard the sound of wolves on the wind.\n4\tTalk to Bounder Primstone outside Oatbarton\tYou have arrived at the outskirts of Oatbarton with Bounder Primstone.\n5\tTalk to Bill Ferny outside Oatbarton\tBill Ferny is on the outskirts of Oatbarton, and if you know him, the Man is up to no good.\n6\tTalk to Bounder Primstone outside Oatbarton\tBounder Primstone is outside Oatbarton.\n",
[7467]="7003E2A3\n1\tTalk to Quickbeam outside the ring of Isengard\tYou have come to the ring of Isengard with as many of the Ents that responded to your call. The time has come to remind Saruman of what he has forgotten!\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam in front of the gate to Isengard\tThe Ents have torn down the gate that gives entrance to the Ring of Isengard.\n3\tPass through the ruined gate of Isengard and defeat Saruman's forces\tThe Ents have smashed open the gate to Isengard, and now you should proceed into the ring.\n4\tThe Ents have been driven mad by the fires of Saruman! His evil must be washed away!\tSaruman has fought back with flame and smoke!\n5\tSurvey your handiwork and greet the newcomer\tThe Ents have diverted the river and flooded the Ring of Isengard. Their purpose: to wash it clean of Saruman's filth.\n6\tSaruman's servant has gone to join his master in the tower\tSaruman's servant has gone to join his master in the tower.\n",
[7468]="7003E2A4\n1\tTalk to Treebeard and listen to his tale\tTreebeard is near the base of Orthanc, and has agreed to finish the story begun by Merry.\n2\tTalk to Treebeard by the base of Orthanc\tTreebeard is by the base of Orthanc.\n",
[7469]="70033962\n1\tTalk to Elrohir on the road through Tûr Morva\tElrohir is waiting to speak with you on the road up the hill in Tûr Morva.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan in Tûr Morva\030Talk to Golodir up the hill in Tûr Morva\030Talk to Calenglad by the entrance to the ruins atop the hill\tSaeradan is north-east of Elrohir, in Tûr Morva. Golodir is up the hill in Tûr Morva. Calenglad is by the entrance to the ruins. Elrohir is pleased that you have decided to leave Tâl Methedras at last and thinks the others will be similarly pleased.\n3\tTalk to Radanir in Tûr Morva, south of Calenglad\tRadanir is among the buildings atop the hill in Tûr Morva. Radanir has returned from his expedition in the mountains.\n4\tAwait the gathering of the Dúnedain atop the hill in Tûr Morva\tThe time has come to decide what each member of the Grey Company should do in the coming days.\n5\tThe Rangers have gathered atop the hill in Tûr Morva. You have helped Radanir fight off a small group of the Falcon Clan, and should now give the Grey Company some of the direction they seek by speaking with Prestadír.\t\n",
[7470]="700479F5\n1\tTalk to nice Master\tThe nice master is near the top of the Winding Stair, looking out upon the dead city below.\n2\tClimb the final stair with the hobbitses\tThere is one more stair to climb before the hobbitses can put the Winding Stair behind them. And then?\n3\tTalk to nice Master\tThe nice Master and the other hobbit need to rest.\n4\tLie down and get some sleep, as the nice Master requested\tThe nice master has asked you to lie down, at least for a little while.\n5\tWait until the hobbitses are deep in conversation\tWait for the hobbitses to become absorbed in their conversation.\n6\tSneak to the east, towards the tower, precious\tYou have business ahead. Leave the hobbitses behind and go to the east, beneath the tower.\n7\tTalk to Sméagol, precious\tSméagol is here. What does he want? Why is he in my way, gollum, gollum?\n8\tSneak to the east, towards the tunnel, gollum\tThe tunnel lies ahead. You need to go there, precious, and make certain all is ready!\n9\tTalk to Sméagol and tell him this will retrieve the Precious\tSméagol is back. He doesn't have the nerve to get the Precious!\n10\tSneak east to the tunnel, precious\tShe will help us get the Precious, yes she will, gollum, gollum!\n11\tTalk to Sméagol outside the tunnel\tSméagol is back, and he wants to keep us from the Precious! Only we know what we must do, gollum!\n12\tEnter the tunnel, gollum, gollum!\tWe have to tell Her what we have brought. She will be so pleased, gollum, gollum!\n13\tFind Her, precious, and tell Her what we have brought!\tWe have to find Her, and tell her what we have brought with us!\n",
[7471]="70033965\n1\tTalk to Radanir by the stopped waggon\tRadanir has sensed something is wrong, and he is standing by the stopped waggon.\n2\tSurvive your second encounter with the oath-breakers\tShades of the oath-breakers you encountered on the Forsaken Road have appeared all around you! What evil do they pose to you now?\n3\tHabla con Britou\tBritou stands before you, a figure of malice that has caused you grief in the recent past. You cannot forgive him, but he appears to offer you no immediate threat.\n4\tAllow the oathbreakers to pass\tThe oathbreakers fade from your sight, returning to the Mountain from which they fled.\n5\tHabla con Radanir\tRadanir has had an idea, and wants to tell it to you.\n6\tTalk to Radanir along the Forsaken Road\tRadanir is beneath the earth along the Forsaken Road.\n7\tYou should find the bodies of your fallen friends and pay your respects, and Radanir will begin carrying them out of the Forsaken Road.\t\n8\tTalk to Radanir along the Forsaken Road, where Candaith fell\tYou have honoured your kinsmen, and should now speak with Radanir along the Forsaken Road.\n",
[7472]="70041244\n1\tExamine Artamir's supplies and contemplate 'The Passage of the Marshes'\tYou stare at the supplies Artamir brought to the Dead Marshes and wonder if Frodo took this treacherous route after all.\n2\tExamine the supplies Artamir brought to the Dead Marshes, and break from your reverie concerning Frodo\tArtamir brought many supplies with him to the Dead Marshes. If Frodo did pass this way, he would not have had as many. What hardships might he have faced on this road?\n",
[7473]="700339A5\n1\tReturn to the entrance of the prison-caves\tThe entrance to the prison-caves of Tûr Morva is to the north-east.\n2\tTalk to Corunir outside the prison-caves\tCorunir is waiting before the entrance to the prison-caves. He must know your mind.\n3\tTalk to Corunir outside the prison-caves... again\tCorunir refuses to let you enter the prison-caves in search of Lheu Brenin.\n4\tTalk to Corunir inside the prison-caves\tCorunir has decided to accompany you into the prison-caves in search of Lheu Brenin.\n5\tTalk to Maelona in the prison-caves\tMaelona has requested your help deep within the prison-caves.\n6\tDrop into the pit at the bottom of the prison-caves\tLheu Brenin has left Dunland and passed into Rohan with those loyal to him, but before he left he cast dissenting members of the Falcon Clan into the Pit of the Falcon at the bottom of the prison-caves.\n7\tTalk to Wenda\tYou have dropped into the pit at the bottom of the prison-caves, where members of the Falcon Clan who displeased Lheu Brenin have been abandoned.\n8\tDefeat the Beast in the Pit\tSomething lives in the bottom of the pit where Lheu Brenin throws his captives.\n9\tTalk to Corunir in the pit\tYou have survived your encounter with the Beast in the Pit, and should see how Corunir is doing.\n10\tTalk to Wenda\tWenda is frightened, but it has been a long time since you were adept with comforting words.\n",
[7474]="7005278E\n1\tTalk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús\tGrimbeorn is outside the Beorninghús.\n2\tHelp Grimbeorn with 'Shades in the Swamp: Ghostly Figures'\tGrimbeorn is outside the Beorninghús.\n3\tHelp Badwila with 'Shades in the Swamp: Vagári the Wanderer'\tEurik's son Badwila is in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.\n4\tHelp Gandalf with 'Shades in the Swamp: The Wanderer Sought'\tGandalf is inside the Beorninghús.\n5\tHelp Gultháva with 'Shades in the Swamp: The Maiden of Gladden'\tGultháva, the Maid of the Gladden, is by the rocky path that leads into the Gladdenmere.\n6\tHelp Gultháva with 'Shades in the Swamp: Only Half-Remembered'\tGultháva, the Maid of the Gladden, is by the ruins of Kidzul-kâlah along the path that runs through Gladdenmere.\n7\tTalk to the Shade of Isildur\tThe shade of Isildur waits on Tol Send, lost within his memories.\n8\tTalk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús\tGandalf is inside the Beorninghús.\n",
[7475]="700339A4\n1\tTalk to Barkh and receive your orders\tYou have been told to report to Barkh in the kitchens for the day's orders.\n2\tTip over the slop bucket\tBarkh wants you to serve some slop to the hungry uruks, but you have a better idea.\n3\tBarkh is not pleased with you\tBarkh is not pleased with your defiance.\n4\tTip over the other slop bucket\tBarkh has asked you one more time to comply with his orders.\n5\tSurvive the consequences of your defiance\tYou have showed your defiance yet again, and the Uruks are not pleased!\n6\tTalk to Gun Ain in the kitchens below Isengard\tGun Ain has come to the kitchens underneath Isengard to bring you before Saruman.\n7\tYou have come with Gun Ain to the tower of Orthanc, there to speak with Saruman.\t\n8\tYou have been brought before the Wizard Saruman.\t\n",
[7476]="700379F7\n1\tTalk to Gléowine on the field of victory, and complete 'Interlude: The Doorward'\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Gléowine has offered to tell you the tale of Háma's heroic last stand before the gates of the Hornburg.\n2\tTalk to Gléowine on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. You have heard his tale of Háma, and should speak now to Gléowine.\n3\tTalk to Théoden on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Théoden is on the field of victory, before the walls at Helm's Deep.\n",
[7477]="70037DBD\n1\tPosition yourself before the door and let no enemies pass\tHáma stands in the gate-house. He has only one door to guard, the door that safe-guards his king.\n2\tTriumph against the Orcs that threaten the Hornburg\tHáma has only one door to guard, the door that safe-guards his king.\n3\tDraw upon reserves of strength by focusing on the glory of Rohan\tHáma must draw upon thoughts of Rohan if he is to persevere.\n4\tStand against the Orcs that threaten the Hornburg\tHáma has only one door to guard, the door that safe-guards his king.\n5\tDraw upon reserves of strength by focusing on the House of Eorl\tHáma must draw upon thoughts of the House of Eorl if he is to persevere.\n6\tSurvive against the Orcs that threaten the Hornburg\tHáma has only one door to guard, the door that safe-guards his king.\n7\tDraw upon reserves of strength by thinking of your father Léoferth\tHáma must draw upon thoughts of his father Léoferth if he is to persevere.\n8\tLive as long as you are able, for Théoden and for Rohan\tHáma has only one door to guard, the door that safe-guards his king.\n",
[7478]="70068273\n1\tTalk to Corudan and go with him on one more journey\tCorudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n2\tTalk to Corudan at the Harbour Warden's tower\tCorudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n",
[7479]="70068274\n1\tTalk to Corudan and go with him to see a lost friend\tCorudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n2\tTalk to Corudan at the Harbour Warden's tower\tCorudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n",
[7480]="7003E295\n1\tTalk to Merry and hear the story of how he met Treebeard\tMerry is outside the gate of Isengard. Merry has agreed to tell you the story of how he and Pippin met Treebeard the Ent.\n2\tTalk to Merry outside the gate of Isengard\tMerry is outside the gate of Isengard.\n",
[7481]="7003E296\n1\tLearn the nature of the curious little creatures\tYou have heard the sound of two curious creatures speaking to one another, and should investigate.\n2\tLearn the nature of the curious little creatures\tThe creatures seem to offer no threat, but you have not seen their like before.\n3\tTalk to one of the curious creatures\tOne of the curious creatures wishes to speak with you. How peculiar.\n4\tTalk to the other hobbit\tThe other hobbit wishes to speak with you.\n5\tLleva a tus nuevos amigos hobbits a la Sala del Manantial\tYou have decided to show these curious little creatures, these hobbits, to your home.\n6\tTalk to Pippin and tell him your house is near\tOne of your new hobbit friends, Pippin, wants to speak with you.\n7\tShow your new hobbit friends the way to your home\tYou have decided to show the hobbits to your home.\n8\tPick up the container of Ent-draught\tYour new hobbit friends may enjoy a sip of Ent-draught.\n9\tYou should pick up two bowls for your hobbit friends and one for yourself.\t\n10\tBring the bowls of Ent-draught to your new hobbit friends\tYour hobbit friends could use a sip of Ent-draught. You should bring them the bowls you picked up.\n11\tWait for your new hobbit-friends to finish drinking the Ent-draught\tThe hobbits seem to be enjoying the Ent-draught.\n12\tHabla con Merry en la Sala del Manantial\tMerry wishes to speak with you about something.\n13\tViaja al Valle Emboscado con los hobbits\tYou have called a moot of your people to decide what is to be done concerning Saruman.\n14\tTalk to Pippin on the way to Derndingle\tYou have brought the hobbits to Derndingle, where the Ents will discuss the matter of Saruman. You should tell the young one what to expect.\n15\tFollow the hobbits to Derndingle\tMany of your people have come to Derndingle to discuss the matter of Saruman.\n16\tConvince Baldbark that something must be done\tBaldbark needs to be convinced.\n17\tConvince Beechbone that something must be done\tBeechbone needs to be convinced.\n18\tConvince Quickbeam that something must be done\tQuickbeam needs to be convinced.\n19\tCapítulo 5: La reunión de la Compañía Gris\tYou should tell the hobbits that Quickbeam will go with them while the moot continues.\n",
[7482]="7003396A\n1\tTalk to Saeradan outside the gates of Lhanuch\tSaeradan is standing outside the gates of Lhanuch and wishes to speak with you.\n2\tTalk to Glynn Brenin at the top of the village\tGlynn Brenin can be found near the top of the village, in front of his dwelling.\n3\tTalk to Anirin down the hill in Lhanuch\tAnirin can be found down the hill in Lhanuch. Anirin, the messenger of the Falcon Clan who has been recovering in Lhanuch from a leg injury, should be told what has happened in Tûr Morva.\n4\tTalk to Suvulch at the west-gate of Lhanuch\tSuvulch of the Uch-lûth is by the gate, confronting a large and hostile force of Dunlendings.\n5\tTalk to Anirin\tThe Dragon Clan has offered Anirin a chance to share in the treasure taken from Lhanuch. Talk to him at the West gate of the village.\n6\tTalk to Glynn Brenin atop the village\tGlynn Brenin is near the top of Lhanuch, fighting off warriors of the Dragon Clan.\n7\tThe Dragon Clan has released worms throughout Lhanuch, and Glynn Brenin wants you to defeat them!\t\n8\tTalk to Saeradan outside the gates of Lhanuch\tSaeradan is outside the gates of Lhanuch. Now that the Dragon Clan has been driven away from Lhanuch, you should speak with Saeradan.\n",
[7483]="70048CDC\n1\tFind the hobbitses!\tFrodo has agreed to tell you the truth of the events within Mount Doom.\n2\tKill the fat hobbit!\tFrodo has agreed to tell you the truth of the events within Mount Doom.\n3\tGet the Ring!\tFrodo has agreed to tell you the truth of the events within Mount Doom.\n4\tThe Precious is ours! Dance, Precious, dance!\tFrodo has agreed to tell you the truth of the events within Mount Doom.\n5\tNo, Precious! Don't leave me!\tFrodo has agreed to tell you the truth of the events within Mount Doom.\n6\tThe Ring is gone\tFrodo has agreed to tell you the truth of the events within Mount Doom.\n",
[7484]="7003FDBF\n1\tTalk to Rovalang and experience 'Interlude: Those Who Are Dead'\tRovalang stands on the slope of the Hill of Erech. Rovalang wishes to learn more of the meeting between the Dead and Aragorn, if you are willing to speak to him.\n2\tTalk to Rovalang\tRovalang is on the slope of the Hill of Erech.\n",
[7485]="7002F936\n1\tHabla con Swithorne en su tienda cerca del Salón del Hidromiel\030Habla con Eldora en su casa cerca de la entrada oeste de Cliving\030Habla con Wigfugol en su finca en la parte noroeste de Cliving\tCada uno de los sospechosos puede encontrarse dentro de la ciudad de Cliving: Swithorne en las tiendas de los Rohirrim junto al Salón del Hidromiel, Eldora en su casa junto a la puerta oeste, y Wigfugol en su finca en la parte noroeste de la ciudad. Walnoth desea que interrogues a las personas que él cree que son los principales sospechosos de los crímenes que han ocurrido.\n2\tRegresa con Walnoth y discute el testimonio de cada sospechoso\tWalnoth puede encontrarse cerca de la fuente en el centro de Cliving. Walnoth espera los resultados de tus interrogatorios.\n",
[7486]="700077DC\n1\tHabla con Second-watcher Heathstraw\tEl segundo vigilante Heathstraw se encuentra cerca de la Fuente del Jabalí en el centro de la Plaza del Mercado en Bree. Lolo Wendingway mencionó que el segundo vigilante Heathstraw podría tener información sobre personas que necesitan cosas hechas en Bree.\n",
[7487]="7006BEAD\n1\tDerrota a los Orcos en Sar-kidul (total: 6)\030Derrota a los Orcos en Ab-dâna (total: 6)\tShukûri has asked that you go to Sar-kidul and Ab-dâna to the north near Utug-bûr to see what you find and defeat any Orcs you encounter there.\n2\tReturn to Shukûri\tReturn to Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe to inform her you have reduced the number of Orcs in the camps near Utug-bûr.\n",
[7488]="70054F40\n1\tFind the entrance of Falch Gurth\tFalch Gurth can be found to the south of Taen Orwath. Cuilion has asked you to enter Falch Gurth and learn what has become of Nidhlas and his men.\n2\tSearch for Nidhlas and his men in Falch Gurth\tFalch Gurth can be found to the south of Taen Orwath. You have entered Falch Gurth in search of Nidhlas and his men. You should continue searching for signs of them.\n3\tFind the source of the voices in Falch Gurth\tThe source of the voices seems to be coming from a raised cleft within Falch Gurth. While exploring Falch Gurth, you overheard hushed voices from the east. You should investigate the source of the voices.\n4\tTalk to Taurdir\tTaurdir can be found at Torgris. You have discovered a small encampment of Rangers within a cleft of Falch Gurth. You should talk to Taurdir.\n",
})
